{"id": "EUVD-2026-84216", "enisaUuid": "ced9d824-c12d-3c04-9494-a0395fcd678f", "description": "vLLM versions through 0.29.0 contain a denial of service vulnerability in the NIXL connector's metadata handling for prefill/decode disaggregated deployments. Attackers can send requests with incomplete kv_transfer_params dictionary entries to trigger an uncaught KeyError in EngineCore scheduling, causing the decode engine to terminate and making all routed requests fail until manual restart.", "datePublished": "2026-09-21T22:04:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-22T13:01:33", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54807", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.29.0/vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/nixl/metadata.py#L294-L312", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vllm-through-0.29.0-denial-of-service-via-incomplete-nixl-kv-transfer-metadata"], "aliases": ["PYSEC-2026-4004", "GHSA-4h5x-w852-6g2x", "CVE-2026-94622"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.63, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02e13814-07df-3528-bf7c-c7d2e944b516", "product": {"name": "vllm", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.29.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8a7c9d42-5850-3236-affe-09e7bd4f6b13", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}], "isExploited": false}